# Architecture & Development Rules: Dhiwa's Personal Portfolio

This document establishes the official architectural rules, coding standards, styling conventions, and SEO requirements for building Dhiwa Thatsbih Azzaraqi's personal branding portfolio website.

---

## 1. Project Directory Structure
All development files must conform to the following clean directory structure:

```
portofolioDhiwa/
├── assets/
│   ├── logos/              # Organization & news site logos (KabaSumbar, PT Homecareku, etc.)
│   ├── screenshots/        # High-quality visual screenshots of portfolio systems
│   └── icons/              # SVG social and stack icons
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # Custom CSS additions (extends Tailwind utilities if needed)
├── insight/
│   ├── architecture.rules  # [Active] Architectural guidelines and requirements
│   └── aboutme.md          # [Proposed] Distilled professional copy, achievements, and metadata
├── js/
│   └── app.js              # Vanilla JS for interactive components (menu toggles, scroll animation)
├── index.html              # Main SEO-optimized entry point
└── tailwind.config.js      # Tailwind configurations (colors, fonts, gradients, glassmorphism)
```

---

## 2. Core Technical Rules

### A. Styling & Frameworks (Tailwind CSS)
*   **Utility First**: Use **Tailwind CSS** for all responsive layouts, typography, and spacing.
*   **Unified Visual Identity**:
    *   **Theme**: Modern Light-to-Dark slate layouts with dynamic Glassmorphism.
    *   **Color Palette**: Harmonious Violet & Soft Indigo (`violet-600`, `indigo-500`) as primary accents, contrasted by Deep Navy (`slate-900`) for the footer and visual depth.
    *   **Glassmorphism**: Use `bg-white/70 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20` for floating cards and the sticky navigation header.
*   **Responsiveness**: The site must be completely responsive. Use standard mobile-first media queries (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).

### B. Structural Semantics & Accessibility
*   **Semantic HTML5**: Always use clean, semantic wrappers: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section id="...">`, `<article>`, `<footer>`.
*   **Heading Hierarchy**: Exactly one `<h1>` per page. Follow a logical sequential heading tree (`<h2>` for major sections, `<h3>` for cards/sub-sections).
*   **ARIA Accessibility**: Include `aria-label`, `aria-hidden`, and keyboard-accessible navigation hooks on interactive elements.

### C. Impeccable SEO Engine Optimization (Local News Standards)
Given Dhiwa's background in local news writing and SEO management, this website must act as a showcase of perfect technical SEO:
*   **Title Tags**: Optimized, keyword-targeted titles containing the name and core specialty.
*   **Meta Description**: Engaging, 150-160 character meta description containing high-value keywords ("D4 Rekayasa Perangkat Lunak", "Software Engineer", "Laravel", "Flutter").
*   **Open Graph / Twitter Cards**: Full metadata integration for standard social sharing previews (title, image, description, site URL).
*   **Image Alt Text**: Every image, screenshot, or brand logo must have a descriptive, SEO-optimized `alt` tag (e.g., `alt="Logo KabaSumbar.net Berita Online Sumatra Barat"`).
*   **JSON-LD Schema Markup**: An embedded `<script type="application/ld+json">` representing `Person` and `CreativeWork` (Portfolio items) for rich Google search result snippet generation.

---

## 3. Dynamic Interactive Rules
To maintain the feel of a modern, elite web application:
1.  **Performance Priority**: Minimize heavy JavaScript packages. All UI mechanics must rely on lightweight, fast **Vanilla JavaScript**.
2.  **Navigation Interactions**: 
    *   Smooth scroll to all sections.
    *   Active navigation tracking (highlighting the menu link corresponding to the current screen scroll position).
3.  **Scroll Animations**: Use CSS keyframes or lightweight Intersection Observers to fade and slide up components beautifully as the user scrolls.

---

## 4. Asset Guidelines
*   **No Placeholders**: Never use placeholder images. Generate exact visual assets matching the actual systems (e.g., the Flutter GS app, Laravel Homecareku platform) to maximize authority and visual impact.
*   **Asset Names**: Maintain lowercase, underscore-delimited names (`homecareku_laravel_mockup.png`, `gs_flutter_app.png`).

---

## 5. Personal Branding & Content Philosophy

### A. Opening Mindset
A portfolio website isn't just a boring digital CV. It's a machine for "selling" and validating your skills. Systematically, it is a combination of a robust work showcase (*Personal CMS*) and a highly conversion-focused marketing funnel (*Mini-CRM*).

### B. The Three Pillars of Personal Branding
To build a strong and resilient *personal brand*, the portfolio design and copy must strictly focus on these three pillars:

1.  **In-Depth Technical Evidence**: 
    *   Don't just display generic images of the interface. Dissect the architectural design.
    *   Showcase your application's MVC structures and systems.
    *   Highlight specific quantitative accomplishments—such as in-depth research on *Deep Learning* architecture or training an Indonesian *Text-to-Speech* model to millions of iterations.
    *   This technical depth is what separates an *Expert* from a regular coder.
2.  **Build an Authentic Persona**:
    *   Technology is rigid, so be human.
    *   Adopt a "big brother" (familiar mentor) persona approach.
    *   Combine sharp coding tutorials/breakdowns with relatable, honest conversations or life advice.
    *   This emotional connection is what keeps your audience loyal and keeps your brand top of mind.
3.  **Measure and Convert**:
    *   Install analytics on your website to track engagement metrics.
    *   Analyze which projects your visitors are reading and interacting with the most.
    *   Direct user interest directly to a clear contact form to secure recruitment or collaboration opportunities.

### C. Closing Philosophy
If an outlet audit system (like `Apl_GS`) is designed to validate the quality of physical retail outlets...
Then a personal portfolio is designed to validate your quality in the eyes of the world. 
Showcase your skills, build rapport, and let the system do the rest.

